PATCH 641: preserve the original0f64 WORD task-status store (board:0009).

Original0f64..0f75 stores DWORD EDX at0d82, loads the full current-task
pointer from0c93 into EBX, executes66 c7 03 ff ff (MOV WORD[EBX],ffff),
and jumps to0f57. The decompile's undefined1 pointer lost the operand
width, so *DAT_0000_0c93=ffff writes only BYTEff. Preserve the existing
pointer owner and explicitly write undefined2; do not widen the pointer
macro used by byte-addressed TCB fields elsewhere.

Both original find/open pairs in tools/oracle/file{,_open}_error_case.json
prove exact whole16MiB reason/status changes before0f57. The original
nonlocal continuation is separately recovered in file_error_main_case.json.
Four reaching Native/WASM6032 failures use real DOS find/open/CF and
observe after the actual0f64 stores, before the unaccepted return/exit.
They require the complete guarded TCB (only the first WORD changes),
source reason, unchanged guarded destination and actual DOS commands.
No observer supplies an I/O/CF/store result.

This restores the task-store width only. Original nonlocal0f57/0f5d,
e339/CRT/main-loop carry, actualop44 dispatch, GP/flags/stack/instruction/
device time and complete original frame/mixedPCM output remain required.
--- a/fist_ext.c
+++ b/fist_ext.c
@@ -1628,7 +1628,7 @@
 
 {
   DAT_0000_0d82 = param_1;
-  *DAT_0000_0c93 = 0xffff;
+  *(undefined2 *)DAT_0000_0c93 = 0xffff;
   return;
 }
 
